# Images: NEVER push raster screen captures to GitHub.
#
# A frame off the emulator carries other players' names and clan tags, the
# owner's own base and gem/loot counters. Those bytes must never enter the
# object database: a blob stays reachable from the public repo after it is
# untracked, so "deleted later" is not deleted. Real frames the gates use live
# on the developer's disk only, and every gate that reads one skips when it is
# absent (corpus_test.go, classifier_fastpath_test.go, classifier_bench_test.go,
# troop_counter_test.go, zz_720p_count_test.go, battle_end_test.go, loot_test.go)
# — run `make test` locally, where the frames still exist, for the real coverage.
#
# Carve-outs below are functional code inputs (template crops, an icon, the one
# sanitized result frame), never full-screen captures:
#   assets/templates/**/*.png                  — gocv template matcher, runtime
#   internal/game/testdata/screen_defeat.png   — defeat fixture, opponent name
#                                                strip blacked out at the source
#   web/src/assets/images/clashgo-logo.png     — UI logo
#   build/appicon.png                          — bundle icon
#
# Before adding any PNG, ask whether it is a capture. If it is, keep it local
# and let the gate skip instead.
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.bmp
**/*.tiff
!**/assets/templates/**/*.png
!internal/game/testdata/screen_defeat.png
!web/src/assets/images/clashgo-logo.png
!build/appicon.png
assets/templates/debug/
assets/templates_captured/
assets/grab/
test_data/
dashboard_ui.png
*.vtest.json

# Auto-generated bindings (do not commit)
web/wailsjs/
web/dist/
web/node_modules/
web/package.json.md5

